sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila ficusphila longitudinal sex-comb Turing wavelength at 2.1 µm — MorphoEval overall 80.7/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg–Turing dispersion at 2.072 µm on a periodic 8×6-wavelength patch, checks the equal-diffusion control analytically (σ_c = -0.1), and fits Euler growth rates to the closed-form eigenvalue (Pearson r = 0.99999994, RMSE = 5.2e-4). The GIF is 16 frames at 800×600. Computer-vision similarity of the last frame to the gallery plate is 81.9. Missing on this pass: a continuous D_u sweep, a simulated ablation field, mask-restricted specimen measurements, and a KS comparison. Overall 80.7/100 (faithfulness 78.7, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ficusphila-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 554243 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 5ea19a1840fdec60e407c004537879eed3753ba0cd5474d1659ab402b161b803 (sha256 5ea19a1840fdec60e407c004537879eed3753ba0cd5474d1659ab402b161b803), spec_fingerprint c6f261396b638d86a346006a062997a1c76d65fe1cbe8f6278c90ec0b2a806df. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c6f261396b638d86a346006a062997a1c76d65fe1cbe8f6278c90ec0b2a806df; artifact_sha256: 5ea19a1840fdec60e407c004537879eed3753ba0cd5474d1659ab402b161b803; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ficusphila_specimen.jpg=8a0ea6252701fd69..., datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=bb3981fcb66333ba..., datasets/drosophila_ficusphila_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=26d1e013287e2844...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952): a reaction-diffusion system can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg (1979): two-species kinetics with a homogeneous steady state and a limit-cycle regime; the Jacobian used here is the standard linearisation of R_u = a - u + u^2 v, R_v = b - u^2 v. | Tanaka, Barmina & Kopp (2009): longitudinal sex combs evolve by about 90 degrees of rotation of a transverse row, or by bristles that arise already longitudinal. | Tanaka et al. (2011) and Kopp (2011): sex-comb teeth are a recent, sex-specific bristle innovation under doublesex and Scr.; reconstructed_in_script: The assigned detail-tier wavelength λ_c = 2.072 µm (2.072e-6 m, log10 = -5.684) is imposed by choosing D_u at diffusion ratio 20. | Predecessor D. eugracilis is given linear density 2/3 and successor D. grimshawi density 1/2, at geological age 0 Ma, producing λ = 3.108 µm and 4.144 µm. | Spiral charge m = 2 is a render choice so the growing mode has the same two-arm layout as the gallery plate.; transfer_boundary: No cited sex-comb paper reports a 2.072 µm Turing wavelength, a Schnakenberg parameter table, or a measured tooth-ridge spacing at this tier. | The chronoseries order (eugracilis before ficusphila before grimshawi) is the project series of extant species, not a stratigraphic lineage.; does_not_claim: That the gallery plate is an SEM or a light micrograph of a sex-comb tooth. | That 2.072 µm was measured on D. ficusphila cuticle. | That the 100 µm sibling slot's alpha/beta power law is this model.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1 parameter-regime sweep: vary D_u over at least eight values at fixed Jacobian and show that λ_c is monotone in sqrt(D_u), and draw that curve.",
            "remediation needed: R2 negative control: integrate the equal-diffusion PDE (D_u = D_v) from the same spiral seed and report that the field variance collapses, next to the analytic σ_c = -0.1.",
            "remediation needed: R3 specimen CV segmentation: border-contrast mask on the real gallery plate; report foreground fraction, circularity and structure-tensor coherency for the plate and for the GIF last frame, with value != reference.",
            "remediation needed: R4 goodness-of-fit: Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic between plate and simulation luminance, plus a finer k-grid so the numeric wavelength is close to 2.072 µm but not copied onto the reference.",
            "remediation needed: R5 single assessor: this pass is builder-scored. A second provider is not available in this run; do not invent one." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.807"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
}

